603 0 obj
<<
/Title (The small, heterogeneous sample of 13 professionals limits transferability and cannot represent women leaders in India or internationally. Interview notes varied in detail and were not audio-recorded or uniformly transcribed, limiting the reliability of quoted wording and the ability to revisit context. The sampling strategy, and geographic coverage, participant demographics, and interview procedures require fuller reporting. Recall and social-desirability effects uneven)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 445 0 R
/Next 604 0 R
>>
endobj
604 0 obj
<<
/Title (Future research could use a transparent sampling strategy and, with appropriate consent, audio recordings or validated interview transcripts across industries, geographic contexts,  career stages. Quantitative measures could be introduced to assess constructs identified in this exploratory study. Comparative organisational studies could examine mento-   -ring, sponsorship, psychological safety, fair recognition. Mixed-methods research could further examine about the proposed framework using validated measures alongside qualitative accounts, and while retaining the attention to experiences that do not fit a single narrative.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 445 0 R
/Prev 603 0 R
>>
endobj
