/Title (The impostor phenomenon is often used to interpret professional self-doubt, but it should not be presumed to apply to every experienced woman professional. Bravata et al. \(2020\) review evidence on its prevalence and correlates, including associations with depression, and the anxiety, job performance, job satisfaction, and burnout across employee groups, including clinicians. This study therefore explores)
